{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/599308-monsters-that-can-turn-into-or-control-swarms-of-rats","id":599308,"title":"Monsters that can turn into or control swarms of rats?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-22T06:45:01-07:00","id":599308,"title":"Monsters that can turn into or control swarms of rats?","content":"Hey there. I've been out of the World of Darkness loop for some time. I never fully got into the various new lines, but I got all the &quot;generic&quot; World of Darkness stuff as it came out. Recently, I ran a Hunter one-shot for my players and they loved it. So it looks like I'm back in the game. Here's the thing, though: since I haven't been following the other WoD lines, I'm not as prepared to create challenges for a Hunter game as I'd like. So help me out here, people who are more knowledgable than me: what are some canon WoD creatures that can turn into or control swarms of rats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7019-bipolarbear","name":"Bipolarbear","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T06:48:12-07:00","id":599329,"title":"","content":"Beshilu (one of the &quot;Host&quot; that Werewolves hunt) literally are swarms of rats in man-suits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T06:54:07-07:00","id":599341,"title":"","content":"Vampires with Animalism.<br /> <br /> Beshilu, probably. <br /> <br /> Rat/Swarm Spirits.<br /> <br /> A mage could probably manage it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T08:13:55-07:00","id":599421,"title":"","content":"Awesome! Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7019-bipolarbear","name":"Bipolarbear","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T10:42:56-07:00","id":599622,"title":"","content":"The vampire swarm form would be my go- to for a quick monster of the week antagonist, bonus points because form swarm is NASTY (protean devotion if i remember correctly)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T15:54:30-07:00","id":599883,"title":"","content":"Beshilu may be the creepiest; imagine attacking the weird, deformed guy who's commanding the rat swarm, only to discover that, instead of blood and organs and the like, he's full of <i>more rats</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T03:32:47-07:00","id":606455,"title":"","content":"I know its unlikely to still be massively relevant but there's also the option of a bespoke rat based Changing Breed. With a little judicious tweeking they can gain a swarm form as one of there alternate forms as well as being able to influence normal animals of there kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7059-brocc013","name":"Brocc013","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T04:56:56-07:00","id":606479,"title":"","content":"This is a common power in both the NWOD and the mythologies that inspire it. In real life, training animals takes discipline, patience and quick wit. Most animals can't be trained at all. So it stands to reason that stories of people and monsters who could control animals like they were moving their own fingers are numerous.<br /> <br /> Vampires with Animalism/Protean, Beshilu and Mages with 2 or more dots in the Life Arcanum can control the behavior of vermin in general (rats, roaches, pigeons). I think you need 3 dots in the Life Arcanum to control mammals, because those are smarter. With 5 dots in Life, you can create living beings out of thin air. Mages with 5 dots in the Fate Arcanum in 1st edition even have access to a spell called Swarm Of Locusts. It causes probability in the area to go bonkers, resulting in things such as traffic accidents like falling dominoes and every rat around start biting everyone. Depending on where you use the spell, you might even &quot;summon&quot; literal locust swarms.<br /> <br /> Prometheans can use various Transmutations of the Disquietism type to control animals' behavior. If you accept roaches instead of rats, Prometheans of the Zeky Lineage often have a Transmutation of the Irradiation type that lets them summon a roach swarm. Another Irradiation Transmutation lets them increase the size of said roaches.<br /> <br /> Changelings in 1st edition have Contracts Of Fang And Talon, and they can buy the Hobgoblin Trainer Merit to have rat monsters with a few powers as protectors. Sin-Eaters have the Primeval Key, which can be combined with 5 dots in the Caul Manifestation to turn you into a rat swarm. Demons have the Swarm Exploit. Mummies have Beast Companion. Werewolves have Nature Gifts and can bargain with the aforementioned Beshilu for their help.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-30-2015, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T05:19:32-07:00","id":606495,"title":"","content":"Pretty much every game line has something. <br /> <br /> Gangrel with protean and animalism. The Beshilu from WtF; I'm sure you could control rats and turn into one with some Gifts. Mages easily pull it off with Life. Prometheans have shapeshifting and animal control powers. Changelings can use Fang and Talon contracts. GtSE uses the Primordial Key. Mummies can use Command the Beast Utterance to force rat swarms to attack. Beast has some Lair traits and the Infestation Avataism. Demons can use Exploits to make hell-rats, you could get a rat-as-Cover, and I think there's a nano-machine-swarm-form that would work as mechanical rat swarm. Hunter doesn't have a PC that does it, but I imagine there's Dread Powers. And that doesn't touch on ephemeral beings with Influence: rats. <br /> <br /> So, that should be your answer - anyone and everyone has the potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}